## Lore

The Metal Morphs are the most fragile of the Haven Mutants. They are born with
frail, misshapen bodies - withered legs, thin arms, soft skulls, long necks -
that grow weaker with age. What keeps them alive is a strange gift: they can
weld scrap metal, wire and parts directly onto their flesh, building a brace of
a shell around a failing body. They are not cyborgs; the metal adds protection
and support but no strength, and a Metal Morph remains feeble, barely able to
walk and no stronger than a child. Onlookers often cannot tell there is a
living being inside the frame at all.

Their strength is the mind: keen intellect, a love of science, and powerful
psionics. Like most Haven Mutants they see themselves as the next step in human
evolution, but they draw a cautious lesson from it. They blame the old world''s
misuse of technology for the Cataclysm, treat science as something dangerous
to be handled with care, and distrust every kind of artificial augmentation -
bionics, drugs, genetic tampering - as a road to lost humanity.

They get on well with Beast Men, whom they try to wean off their dependence on
machines, and with Pseudo Men. They are the Haven Mutants most open to
outsiders, and enjoy long conversations with them. With the Mantis Men they
argue constantly: the Metal Morphs hope the mutants will guide humanity toward
restraint, while the Mantis Men want humanity gone, a view the Metal Morphs fear
could end in genocide. They think well of the White Rose knights and suspect the
magical White Rose means something important they have not yet worked out.

They dislike the Splugorth and their minions, slavers, Horune Pirates and
outsiders who lean heavily on technology, and they rarely leave Madhaven
because they feel too vulnerable outside it.

## Equipment

A Mutant Bone Dagger, one weapon for its W.P. with 1D4 extra E-Clips, a portable
computer and a tool kit, an audio recorder, a sketchbook and four note pads,
1D4+6 markers, a dozen pencils, a sack of 2D6+10 M.D.C. scrap pieces to hurl with
Telekinetic Acceleration Attack, 2D4 days of food and water, a utility belt, a
box of 100 latex gloves, a backpack, a satchel, a canteen, a cigarette lighter, a
cross carved from mutant bone, 1D6 pre-Rifts science or history books (each
worth 1D6x1000 credits to a collector) and personal items. Wears no clothes or
armor.

Money: no credits, but 4D6x1000 worth of tradable goods - old books, disks,
parts and artifacts, or loot from outsiders.

## Mutant Shaman

A large clan is led by a Shaman, who may be of any Haven Mutant race. The
`shaman` variant adds the attribute and P.P.E. bonuses and the Shaman''s skills.
What the app does not apply:

- The Shaman skill list REPLACES all Secondary Skills, Piloting skills and
  modern W.P. skills. A Shaman never uses a modern weapon, vehicle or machine.
  Drop the secondary picks and the modern W.P. by hand.
- Shamans are the clan''s lawgivers, judges and leaders.
- **Prayer of Strength** to Isis, the Mighty Lady: 01-20% +5% per level to be
  heard, up to six times a year. If answered: +6 P.S., +1D4x10 M.D.C., and 48
  hours without food or water with no ill effect.
- **Prayer of Inspiration or Wisdom:** 01-12% +3% per level (+10% after a week
  of fasting). If answered, a dream brings insight, an idea or a warning about
  the matter prayed over.
- A Shaman levels on the Gateway Knight & Mutant Shaman ladder (printed 79):
  0 / 2,351 / 4,701 / 9,401 / 18,801 / 28,001 / 38,001 / 53,001 / 77,001 /
  102,001 / 143,001 / 195,201 / 240,401 / 310,601 / 360,801.

## GM Notes

Average level of experience 1D6+5. Usually met in pairs, alone, or travelling
with a mixed band of other mutants. Alignment is usually Principled (10%),
Scrupulous (30%) or Unprincipled (30%).
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'metal-morph');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'metal-morph';

